    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (1 test class, `AcceptanceTest`) passes and the JaCoCo coverage gate is satisfied \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked that, alongside the existing human-readable audit line, owner creation emit an **immutable structured event** via the `AUDIT` logger: `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`, where `seq` increases monotonically across creates and the event carries the owner's *current primary identifier*.\n\nI made two changes, both localized to the existing `audit` pipeline step (no YAML rewiring needed):\n\n**1. New `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 an immutable `record` (seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event) with a `toJson()` that renders the compact JSON object and a `OWNER_CREATED` constant. Being a record makes the event immutable, as required.\n\n**2. `AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 after the existing audit line, it now builds and logs an `OwnerCreatedEvent`:\n- `seq` comes from a `static AtomicLong SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet()`, so it's monotonic across all creates for the JVM.\n- The identifier value comes from a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` accessor that today returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. That method is the sole hook the future memberId change touches \u2014 when customerCode is unified into memberId, only `primaryIdentifier` changes and the event automatically carries the memberId, exactly as the spec (and the test's forward-looking comment) describe.\n- `membershipLevel` uses `MembershipLevels.of(owner)`, consistent with the value the existing audit line already reports at this pipeline position (the capped transient isn't assigned until a later step).\n\nObserved output during the test run:\n```\nINFO AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe event and the audit line are separate `AUDIT` log entries, so nothing that relied on the existing line changes; the new `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` (asserting one line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode) passes.",
